"id":4014322636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vRbPM","user":{"login":"Josvanegmond","id":1975067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NzUwNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1975067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond","html_url":"https://github.com/Josvanegmond","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Josvanegmond/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T21:44:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T21:44:36Z","body":"> It is indeed not useful for most containers, and even for a lot of interactive controls (like buttons) which have `text`/`title` or similar property that's used as a name.\n\nI did not realize button texts were automatically used by the screen reader and an accessibility name is not needed. It would be nice to have some documentation when and how the accessibility properties should be used. The risk is that we implement it incorrectly and make the screen reader less effective.\n\nThanks for the swift responses and all the work you've put into the accessibility side of Godot!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4014322636/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]